    thermal_tranche_artifact_coverage: { cell: "K", ev: "xiso-5 §1 (47 blank; no online_frac column); xiso-6 2026-08-25 (FINDING-xiso6-tranche-vintage-sidecar-2026-08-25.md): vintage sidecar backfilled + arm-over-gap guard armed at bins_to_fleet — cell UNCHANGED NYISO-175 (2026-09-02, ZERO SOLVE; docs/FINDING-nyiso175-ct-deficit-two-objects-2026-09-02.md section 4.4). CELL UNCHANGED AT O -- and a NAMED, SIZED, FLEET-WIDE ATTRIBUTION DEFECT is added to it, handed forward rather than armed. derive_thermal_tranches._fleet_nameplate_and_group attributes a plant's FACILITY-SUMMED CAMPD net to 'the group holding the most nameplate at each plant'. At a mixed plant that is a guess, and it picks the wrong carrier at THREE NYISO plants in every year, for 15.233 TWh of measured conduct over 2023-2025: Ravenswood (2500) 8.509 TWh -- primary ST_GAS 1,724.8 MW while CC_REGULAR 222.2 MW carries 64-73 % of the energy, a 1,502.6 MW margin picking the wrong bin; East River (2493) 6.581 TWh -- primary ST_CHP 309.5 MW against CT_CHP 306.0 MW carrying 100.0 % of the CAMPD grossLoad, decided by 3.5 MW = 1.1 %; S A Carlson (2682) 0.142 TWh. Consequence at East River: its ST_CHP tranche row carries online_hours 26,253, committed_pct 32.0, p25_cf 67.2 and median_cf 98.5 -- the TURBINE half's measured conduct, on the STEAM half's 309.5 MW denominator -- while the 306.0 MW turbine bin gets no row at all. Same defect family as nyiso-174 section 6 item 1 (_resolve_unit_group's last-writer-wins fac_group short-circuit in the OUTAGE extract) and neiso-99's rule 14 [R-ACCURATE] exception: a per-plant aggregate assigned to one of a mixed plant's classes by a proxy instead of by the units' own meters. The corrected per-unit construction already exists and is tested (scripts/lib/campd_measured_classes.py, nyiso-174). ZERO DOF -- a crosswalk repair, not a re-derivation against a residual, so rule 23 [R-FROZEN-DERIVE] is satisfied by citing the attribution defect. NOT ARMED HERE: the pre-registered gate S3 requires East River to be >= 50 % of the misattributed energy and it is 43.2 %, so the object is fleet-wide and needs a session that can carry a full three-year re-solve (re-deriving the tranche artifact is solve-affecting). EXPECTED VALUE STATED HONESTLY: closing East River's split moves C1 CT_CHP by +0.378 / +0.965 / +0.402 TWh and ST_CHP by -0.064 / -0.343 / -0.713 TWh, and its C3a expectation is ~ZERO -- both bins carry the same heat rate (7.4205, nyiso-120) and the same delivered gas, so moving energy between them changes no marginal cost. Propose it on rule 1 [R-STRUCT] grounds, NEVER as a C3a-2025 lever. It belongs in the same commit as nyiso-174 section 6 item 1. NYISO-175b (2026-09-02, ZERO SOLVE; docs/FINDING-nyiso175b-tranche-attribution-repair-2026-09-02.md; PREREG-nyiso175b-tranche-attribution-repair.md committed at 22bfe37a BEFORE the probe or any derivation ran). CELL MOVES O -> K: the attribution defect this cell has carried as an open object is now REPAIRED IN CODE, validated at artifact level, and shipped DEFAULT-OFF as a companion. derive_thermal_tranches --per-unit-attribution routes each CAMPD unit's gross to the bin that CONTAINS it via campd_measured_classes.corrected_unit_class, writing thermal_tranches-perunit-<ISO>.csv -- never an overwrite, so the off path is byte-inert (the -unitroute- discipline). ALL FOUR PRE-SOLVE GATES PASS. K1: 13.7577 TWh re-seated over 2023-2025 (bar 4.0), 4.5293/4.5612/4.6672 by year, six plants -- East River 6.5811 onto CT_CHP, Ravenswood 5.8467 onto CC_REGULAR, then Bethpage 0.5006 / E F Barrett 0.4570 / Port Jefferson 0.2302 / S A Carlson 0.1422. (Quote 13.7577 for the repair's footprint and nyiso-175's 15.233 for the plants' whole conduct -- different statistics, not a disagreement.) K2 FAILED AS FIRST CONSTRUCTED and forced an amendment to the CONSTRUCTION, never the threshold: three ST_GAS-only plants (2490, 8906, 2516 Northport) have CAMPD combustion turbines correcting to CT_PEAKER, a bin they do not carry, so 0.0051 TWh would have been silently dropped out of the ST_GAS denominator -- a reclassification, not a crosswalk repair. reseat_group now leaves a unit on the plant's primary group wherever the plant carries no bin in its own prime-mover family; re-run PASS (0 offenders over 96 single-thermal-group plants). K3 (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH], measured by CALLING the production resolver): the existing miso-200 mixed_gas_routing gate CANNOT reach East River -- _GAS_BIN_GROUPS excludes both CT classes so {CT_CHP, ST_CHP} intersects at size 1 -- AND is actively WRONG where it does fire, routing Ravenswood's block CTs CT0001/0010/0011 to CT_PEAKER (dropped from the overlay) although those are three of the 27 units the neiso-99 guard's own evidence names as gas-fired block members. K4: all three carrier bins genuinely lack a tranche row today. ARTIFACT DELTA, unconfounded (both legs derived at HEAD): 13 of 85 rows, seven plants. THIS RESOLVES nyiso-174 section 6 item 2 IN THE ARTIFACT -- East River's ST_CHP measured row correctly disappears (boilers generate 0.000 TWh in all three years) and a CT_CHP row appears at 306.0 MW / 26,251 online hours / committed 30.1 / chp_pmin_cf 28.4, moving the must-run to the half the meters say is running; Ravenswood ST_GAS 23,472 -> 7,293 h with a new 222.2 MW CC_REGULAR row at committed 70.0; S A Carlson's 120-hour ST_GAS row is replaced by a 3,913-hour CT_PEAKER row, RECOVERING the committed artifact's own online_hours on the correct bin. ONE NEGATIVE RESULT AT FULL STRENGTH: the physically-impossible median_cf > 100 census improves only 11 -> 10, so above-nameplate CEMS gross is NOT a signature of this defect and must not be quoted as evidence for it. NO LP RAN, and the reason is a NEW BLOCKER, not a judgement about the repair: BOTH NYISO solve inputs are non-reproducible at HEAD. thermal_tranches_NYISO.csv (sidecar derive_invocation null, vintage unknown, its own text saying it 'makes no claim about what HEAD would emit') differs from a fresh unrepaired HEAD derivation on 46 of 78 rows -- online_hours by up to 26,271, median_cf 65.6, committed_pct 27.2 -- and the outage extract is worse in proportion at 4,423 -> 2,632 windows (-40 %). A fully re-derived arm therefore carries the repair AND 40 rows of unadjudicated drift at plants it never touches; the minimal-delta escape ALSO fails, because at two of the seven affected plants the drift EXCEEDS the repair (Bethpage CC_REGULAR drift -2,337 h vs repair -217; E F Barrett ST_GAS drift +3,050 vs repair -736). A clean A/B needs a HEAD control leg -- TWO three-year solves -- and even then the arm is NOT promotable. HANDED FORWARD: adjudicate the drift and re-baseline the keeper's inputs at HEAD FIRST, then land this repair on top as a clean delta. ALSO NOT BUILT: nothing in src/ reads the -perunit- tranche companion -- the path is hardcoded at 11 call sites (campd_bins.py x9, coal.py, chp.py), 9 taking only iso and no config, so a resolver plus a ScenarioConfig field threaded through those callers is required (rule 24). EXPECTED VALUE UNCHANGED AND STATED HONESTLY: C3a-2025 expectation ~ZERO (both East River bins carry heat rate 7.4205 and the same delivered gas), and the prereg's gate K5 FAILS a large favourable C3a move for exactly that reason. Rule 1 [R-STRUCT] grounds only, NEVER a C3a lever." },
