    measured_interface_limits: { cell: "G", ev: "nyiso-109 (refused ex-ante on NYISO's own MIS P-32 flow-vs-limit measurement; results/calibration/_nyiso109_trough_offer_stack.json). RE-CONFIRMED AND STRENGTHENED 2026-09-01 (nyiso-169, ZERO SOLVE, no verdict move): the refusal reproduces off an INDEPENDENT instrument -- NYISO's own posted LBMP congestion component (MCC) rather than the flow-vs-limit record -- and upgrades from 'the posted limits do not bind' to 'the measured congestion is statistically INVARIANT to whether they bind'. Posted cutsets sit within 50 MW of limit in 0.0-0.8% of hours (CENTRAL EAST - VC 0.75/0.13/0.21%; TOTAL EAST, UPNY CONED, SPR/DUN-SOUTH 0.00% in every year -- nyiso-109's CE figures reproduced to the digit), while the posted MCC is non-zero in 4-64% of hours; AT MOST 1.7% of each model link's annual mean congestion arises in a posted-binding hour and on three of four links it is exactly 0.00%. CENTRAL EAST conditional means barely move ($8.98 all-hours vs $8.89 non-binding, 2023). THE KILL GENERALISES BEYOND POSTED LIMITS to the aggregate-TTC mechanism class: a chain link's dual is non-zero only when its own flow is at TTC, and the model OVER-separates the link it under-prices (Upstate_West->Capital_Hudson 82-99% of hours vs a market congested 15-55%) while UNDER-separating the three it misses (0.3-30% vs 4-64%) -- the mechanism's SHAPE is wrong, so no re-estimation of a limit reaches the object. Consequently the zonal-gradient half of C3a (35% of 2025's deficit) is a REPRESENTATION LIMIT at five-zone grain, not a missing mechanism: the market's high-load price surface is non-monotone along the model's radial chain (2025 80-90th pct: Capital_Hudson prices $23.29 ABOVE Upstate_West and $7.54 ABOVE Lower_Hudson), which a four-link chain with aggregate TTCs cannot produce at any setting. Also corrected: nyiso-168 section 5's 'the gradient component is not even consistently signed' is true of the AGGREGATE and false of every component -- decomposed exactly along the chain (identity error 0.00e+00 in all three years) it is four per-link terms each consistently signed 2023-2025 that CANCEL. A zonal congestion adder is NOT proposed and was not built (rule 13 [R-MEASURED]: posted MCC is a measured OUTCOME); tightening a TTC below its measured value is refused on rule 1 [R-STRUCT]. Evidence: docs/FINDING-nyiso169-congestion-gradient-anatomy-2026-09-01.md, results/calibration/_nyiso169_congestion_gradient_anatomy.json, scripts/probes/nyiso169_congestion_gradient_anatomy.py (committed before it was run)." },
